From 558e61e58d6bc3e702a97dea43b80c39d2a820d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 02:48:48 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] test(post): recorded streams carry the work offset as an
 index (#931)

Main's recorded-stream guards (#926) build Dump { wcs: "G54" }; this
slice's dump writes the 1-based index, so the byte-for-byte stream
guards need PARAM WorkOffset 1.000000. Only the stream files were
regenerated (WRITE_GOLDEN=1 on recorded_streams and
recorded_post_streams); every script golden is byte-identical
(offset 1 still posts each dialect's first-offset word).

Refs #931

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL
